Disjunctive == guard: Commit returns release()'s error as is when it is nil or repo.ErrTxDone
(if err == nil || err == repo.ErrTxDone { return err }), otherwise wrapped.
Go semantics: sentinel repo.ErrTxDone bare, and os.Remove's errors ONLY behind (*fs.PathError).Unwrap +
"filerepo: commit: %w".
Recorded: repo.ErrTxDone only bare (the wrap path is filtered correctly), but every os.Remove error twice, once
wrapped and once bare (chain (*fs.PathError).Unwrap only). Not flagged: guards are applied by dominance (plan S07:
"if neither dominates R, the guard doesn't apply on that path"), and neither comparison dominates the body of an
||, so this is a documented, sound over-approximation; nothing is missing. The same shape in os.(*File).wrapErr
(err == nil || err == io.EOF) adds PathError-less variants to every (*os.File) Read/Write set in this app.
The leaves come from closures of other os functions too (os.chmod$1, os.openFileNolog$1, os.checkPidfd$1), which
os.Remove never passes to os.ignoringEINTR: Candidates are not narrowed per caller (plan S09, see
server_openstore_call).
-- args --
-fanout=0 repo/filerepo/filerepo.go:@commit
